NAME
    queue - inspect runner resource slots and acquire a slot prefix

SYNOPSIS
    queue
    queue ask CLASS [--gb N] [--min N] [--as WHO]

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.testing module. Manages per-class execution
    slots configured in ~/.config/EmuSen/testing/runners.json (default
    desktop configuration: two 'cpu' slots and one 'gpu' slot). Slots
    are backed by flock(2) lock files under
    ~/.cache/emusen/testing/queue/. trial(1) automatically acquires cpu
    slots for its concurrent steps.

    With no arguments, prints one tab-separated row per slot: class,
    slot path, state ('held' or 'free'), holder name, and timestamp.

    'queue ask CLASS' blocks until a slot of CLASS is available (or
    until interrupted), logs the request to the store's queue table, and
    prints a command prefix invoking flock(1) on that slot followed by
    'systemd-run --user --scope' with CPUWeight=20, MemoryMax=<gb>G, and
    MemorySwapMax=2G. Running a command after that prefix holds the slot
    for the duration of the command.

OPTIONS
    --gb N
        MemoryMax limit in GiB passed to systemd-run (default: 10).
    --min N
        Accepted by the option parser for compatibility; currently
        ignored.
    --as WHO
        Requester name recorded in the slot lock and queue table
        (default: $USER).

EXAMPLES
    queue
    $(dianash -c 'queue ask cpu --gb 8 --as studio') cargo build --release

EXIT STATUS
    0   Slot table printed or slot prefix acquired.
    2   Unknown subcommand, unknown slot class, invalid option value, or
        interrupted while waiting.

SEE ALSO
    trial(1), results(1)
